<h2>Asobi 0.2 (build 280)</h2>
<p><b>Web reviewers can speak their notes.</b></p>
<ul>
<li>Voice notes from the browser: web reviewers hold the mic button (or V), speak, release — the note lands on the frame they were parked on. Audio uploads encrypted end-to-end and is wiped with the review.</li>
<li>Your Mac does the transcription: the host app fetches the sealed audio, transcribes it on-device with the same speech pipeline as native voice notes, and the text appears for everyone — attributed to the speaker, never sent to any cloud service.</li>
<li>Voice rows in the web comment list play back on click, and show "transcribing…" until the text arrives.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
